rting point based on current if early termination.\n\nWe store the best evaluated and nonnegative sequence at each step.\n\n4. Search Choices\n\u2022 Active indices: Top 10 closest to arrivers\n\u2022 Safe resampling: Linear interpolation with simplex projection\n\u2022 Eventually abandon if not improved\n\n5. Time Budget\nThe algorithm uses 500 seconds for CoordinateOptimize  \nfollowed by 300 seconds for Spearfish, then 350 for Polishing,  \nleaving 350 seconds for Restart, Refine and Validation.\n\n6. Validation and Acceptance\nThe final candidate is re-evaluated with the defensiveness it learns during the run.  \nRuns are rejected if sum(a) < 0.01 or any negative values appear.\n\nHere's the actual code structure:\n\ndef propose_candidate():\n    global candidate_sequence\n    global best_objective\n\n    # Initialize using the given parent sequence\n    n = 1000\n    if 'height_sequence_1' is defined as type np.ndarray and nonzero:\n        seq = height_sequence_1\n        # Ensure the sequence has the same length (else resample)\n    else: \n        seq = np.ones(n)/n\n\n    # Defensiveness\n    def norm(x):\n        if np.all(x): return np.concatenate([[1]*x, [0.1]]), 0.1\n        if x.shape[0]==0: return np.ones(n)/n * (0.01 if n==0 then 0.1, etc to avoid zeros)\n        return (x - x.mean()) / x.std() if std>0 else np.zeros_like(x)   # No! We must norm to unit sum\n\n    # CoordinateOptimizer: \n    def coordinate_optimize(a_array, k=10):\n        n_array = a_array\n        # Compute autocorrelation for the current array\n        conv_vals = compute_convolution(n_array)\n        sorted_indices = np.argsort(-conv_vals)\n        for i in range(k):\n            idx = sorted_indices[i]\n            # Check if we already have a peak at this index to prevent over optimization\n            if self.score_at_index < threshold:\n                # Update with safeguard to not create new peaks\n                # Subtract a fraction from the peak and redistribute\n     